{{also|salvador|Salvádor}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|es|-}} and {{der|en|pt|Salvador}}, chiefly various placenames honoring {{w|Jesus Christ}}, from {{der|en|es|-}} and {{der|en|pt|salvador||[[savior]]}}, from {{der|en|la|salvator}}, from {{m|la|salvo|salvāre|to [[save]]}} + {{m|la|-tor|pos=forming [[agent noun]]s}}. In Spanish placenames, frequently a clipping of {{der|en|es|San Salvador||[[holy|Holy]] [[savior|Savior]]}}. {{doublet|en|savior|Salvator|Salvatore}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsælvədɔː(ɹ)/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Salvador.wav|a=Southern England}}

